        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-04T15:53:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the old code, we did one arena allocation that held the packed IDs and the Glyph* together (as Variant). Now we are still using the arena allocation for the packed IDs but later on doing a heap allocation to store the Glyph* as part of the backend GlyphData.\n\nCan we reuse that storage for the Glyph* addresses even if we allow the backends to set them to the backend-specific Glyphs? I am unsure how often SubRuns are able to be reused to benefit from caching the GlyphData allocations.\n\nIf we don\u0027t want to have the variant, is it possible to plumb the slug\u0027s arena through so that the glyph data can use it as well?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "e31fc410c91e5cefbc668f5acaff1e3822d0faac",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
